    {
      "t": "2026-11-19T00:00:01Z",
      "text": "According to the Joint Organisations Data Initiative, Saudi Arabia's oil exports rose in September to their highest level since the war began in February, despite Houthi attacks on Red Sea ports and infrastructure.",
      "cites": [
        "wiki:2026-11-19:10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "t": "2026-11-19T00:00:08Z",
      "text": "The insurer Allianz Trade announced on 11 November 2026 that the US-Israeli war on Iran would cost Gulf countries more than $200 billion in total, and up to $790 billion by 2030.",
      "cites": [
        "wiki:rev:1386680509:186"
      ]
    },
    {
      "t": "2026-11-19T00:00:15Z",
      "text": "The International Energy Agency has characterized the 2026 Iran war, including the closure of the Strait of Hormuz, as the largest supply disruption in the history of the global oil market.",
      "cites": [
        "wiki:rev:1386680509:0"
      ]
    },
    {
      "t": "2026-11-19T00:00:25Z",
      "text": "The report was published by Al Jazeera.",
      "cites": [
        "wiki:2026-11-19:10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "t": "2026-11-19T00:00:33Z",
      "text": "Al Jazeera's headline read: “Iran war live: Houthis escalate attacks on Saudi capital.”",
      "cites": [
        "news:aljazeera:560937a18abe"
      ]
    },
    {
      "t": "2026-11-19T00:00:39Z",
